","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Council requires escalating annual savings totalling \u00a35.076m (20% of base budget) by 2029/30, with very difficult decisions ahead","lead":"A 20% structural funding cut by 2030 signals severe ongoing financial pressure; the council will need to make strategic choices about which services to maintain or reduce, affecting delivery across the local government sector.","iso":"2026-09-10","paper_title":"Item 7- Community Services and Licensing Budget Monitoring Report Q1 202627","paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20977/20977.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Revenue & Benefits forecasting \u00a352k overspend from staffing misalignment and unbudgeted operational costs","lead":"This reveals a controllable cost problem: the council has not aligned its revenue budgets to actual staffing needs, suggesting wider budget planning or staffing governance issues.","iso":"2026-09-10","paper_title":"Item 7- Community Services and Licensing Budget Monitoring Report Q1 202627","paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20977/20977.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Community Services and Licensing Committee","paper_title":"Item 7- Community Services and Licensing Budget Monitoring Report Q1 202627","paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20977/20977.pdf","headline":"Underlying revenue overspend of \u00a339k is masked by holding back \u00a320k of planned savings in abeyance","detail":"The reported net overspend is only \u00a319k, but this includes \u00a320k of savings 'currently being held' pending the full savings review in September-October workshops. The actual underlying position is \u00a339k overspend. This technique smooths the reported position below the real outturn.","category":"overspend","matters":"The council is using accounting reserves to mask underlying cost pressures, suggesting either higher controllable overspends or a conscious strategy to defer savings decisions to later in the financial year.","figures":"\u00a319k reported net overspend, \u00a320k held savings, \u00a339k underlying overspend","quote":"This is net of a proposed saving of \u00a320k towards the overall savings targetof \u00a320k, currently being held, as set out in Section 5.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Community Services and Licensing Committee","paper_title":"Item 7- Community Services and Licensing Budget Monitoring Report Q1 202627","paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20977/20977.pdf","headline":"Council requires escalating annual savings totalling \u00a35.076m (20% of base budget) by 2029/30, with very difficult decisions ahead","detail":"The Medium Term Financial Plan shows savings requirements rising from \u00a3400k (2%) in 2026/27 to \u00a31,426m (5%) in 2027/28, \u00a32,000m (8%) in 2028/29, and \u00a35,076m (20%) by 2029/30. The council explicitly states these savings requirements will lead to reductions in service delivery and require very difficult decisions.","category":"savings","matters":"A 20% structural funding cut by 2030 signals severe ongoing financial pressure; the council will need to make strategic choices about which services to maintain or reduce, affecting delivery across the local government sector.","figures":"\u00a3400k (2%), \u00a31,426m (5%), \u00a32,000m (8%), \u00a35,076m (20%)","quote":"The size of the savings required mean that very difficult decisions will need to be taken on how the savings targets will be met, and this will lead to reductions in service delivery.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Community Services and Licensing Committee","paper_title":"Item 7- Community Services and Licensing Budget Monitoring Report Q1 202627","paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20977/20977.pdf","headline":"Revenue & Benefits forecasting \u00a352k overspend from staffing misalignment and unbudgeted operational costs","detail":"The service is overspending due to budget misalignment in staffing establishment, recruitment costs, and higher transactional costs in payment processing and postal activities running above budgeted assumptions. This indicates the council's budget does not reflect actual staffing requirements.","category":"overspend","matters":"This reveals a controllable cost problem: the council has not aligned its revenue budgets to actual staffing needs, suggesting wider budget planning or staffing governance issues.","figures":"\u00a352k overspend forecast (approximately \u00a343k controllable)","quote":"The variance is primarily driven by a combination of staffing pressures and higher than budgeted operational costs. Staffing costs reflect budget alignment issues within the establishment, alongside recruitment-related expenditure. There are also ongoing pressures within transactional service costs, particularly payment processing and postal activities, which are forecast to exceed budget assumptions.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Community Services and Licensing Committee","paper_title":"Item 7- Community Services and Licensing Budget Monitoring Report Q1 202627","paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20977/20977.pdf","headline":"Lido maintenance capital programme \u00a3890k underspent (36% shortfall) due to resource constraints","detail":"The Active Lifestyles Stroud & Lido Maintenance budget of \u00a31,700k is forecast to deliver only \u00a3810k in Q1, a \u00a3890k shortfall. The council explicitly confirms the ringfenced budget will not be spent this year because leisure team resource was absorbed by the Lido opening project. This represents a material failure to execute planned capital improvements.","category":"capital","matters":"The council cannot execute a committed capital programme due to resource constraints, suggesting either poor project planning or insufficient staffing to manage multiple concurrent projects.","figures":"\u00a31,700k budget, \u00a3810k forecast, \u00a3890k underspend (36%)","quote":"Work on the Lido has taken all leisure resource during the first half of the financial year but resource is now allocated to progress. This budget is now ringfenced based on committee and council decisions. The budget will not be fully spent by the leisure team this financial year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Community Services and Licensing Committee","paper_title":"Item 7 - Appendix A \u2013 Budget Monitoring Service breakdown","paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20978/20978.pdf","headline":"Youth Services costs have increased 53% mid-year without corresponding budget revision until now","detail":"Youth Services (combined Hear by Right / Youth Services and Youth Services 3.7) shows a forecast of \u00a3187k against a budget of \u00a3122k, a \u00a365k overspend. The reserve transfer of (\u00a365k) indicates this was not anticipated when the revised budget was set.","category":"overspend","matters":"Youth services are a statutory duty in most councils, and cost overruns here may indicate either demand surge or inability to deliver the service within budget, both signalling pressure on core provision.","figures":"Youth Services: \u00a3122k budget \u2192 \u00a3187k forecast (\u00a365k overspend, 53% increase)","quote":"Youth Services 3.7 122 122 187 (65) 0","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-10"},"name":"Stroud","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"Underlying revenue overspend of \u00a339k is masked by holding back \u00a320k of planned savings in abeyance","lead":"The council is using accounting reserves to mask underlying cost pressures, suggesting either higher controllable overspends or a conscious strategy to defer savings decisions to later in the financial year.","also":["8 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Standards Committee on 2026-09-29","n_findings":9,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Item 7- Community Services and Licensing Budget Monitoring Report Q1 202627","top_paper_url":"https://stroud.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s20977/20977.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":78,"news_drafts_total":3}}